 buzzing stocks 
 Stock-specific activity is likely to remain in focus on Dalal Street on October 12, following a slew of corporate developments, bulk deals, earnings and brokerage recomendations.
Lenskart Solutions share price fell nearly 5 percent after 2.93 crore shares (1.67% equity) worth Rs 1,895 crore change hands at Rs 647 per share via block deals.
Viviana Power Tech share price added more than 6 percent after the company secured turnkey contracts worth Rs 466.73 crore from MGVCL for converting 11 kV overhead HT lines into MVCC overhead lines and developing underground network infrastructure.
Can Fin Homes share price surged 5 percent after the company reported a 9.2% year-on-year rise in Q2 profit to Rs 274.6 crore, while net interest income grew 6.65% to Rs 431.5 crore.
Poonawalla Fincorp share price rose 2.5 percent after the company reported a five-fold year-on-year jump in Q2 consolidated profit to Rs 374.85 crore, while net interest income surged 75.7% to Rs 1,589 crore.
Waterways Leisure Tourism share price rose 9 percent after the company reported a Q2 consolidated profit of Rs 58.5 crore against a loss of Rs 8.9 crore a year ago, while revenue grew 30.9% to Rs 132.9 crore.
Suzlon Energy share price jumped 4 percent after MOSL maintained its Buy rating with a target price of Rs 65 per share, noting that the stock has corrected 31% in over three months and is trading at 17.5 times FY28 EPS, 20% below its one-year forward mean minus one standard deviation of 22 times.
Investors are expected to remain focused on brokerage calls, block deals, order wins, regulatory developments and other company-specific triggers that could drive stock-level volatility during the session.
